WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:30.605
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:30.875 --> 00:34.708
- Dante! - Dante!

3
01:36.708 --> 01:38.625
One, two, three.

4
01:39.916 --> 01:40.833
One…

5
02:02.625 --> 02:05.083
Come on! Come on, baby, come on!

6
02:32.208 --> 02:33.624
Hey, Mom.

7
02:33.625 --> 02:36.749
At first I couldn't sleep all night, I was so excited,

8
02:36.750 --> 02:38.499
and then I overslept.

9
02:38.500 --> 02:39.665
No big deal.

10
02:39.666 --> 02:42.624
I hope you have a really, really good first day, sweetie.

11
02:42.625 --> 02:43.708
Thanks.

12
02:44.250 --> 02:47.957
And, you know, Dad would be so proud of you.

13
02:47.958 --> 02:50.499
You're the first woman mechanic at Eagle Racing.

14
02:50.500 --> 02:53.958
I have to hang up, I'm nearly there. Love you. See you later.

15
03:03.416 --> 03:06.458
Eagle Headquarters. You have reached your destination.

16
03:11.916 --> 03:15.916
Hey, watch out! Are you blind or something, you moron?

17
03:18.500 --> 03:20.250
Sorry, Mr. Annunziata!

18
03:20.791 --> 03:21.833
I'm sorry.

19
03:29.500 --> 03:31.665
Hey, Dante, where are you?

20
03:31.666 --> 03:33.957
Have you seen the videos from last night yet?

21
03:33.958 --> 03:35.957
Because people will be talking about them.

22
03:35.958 --> 03:38.000
But let's just stay cool, okay? Later.

23
03:45.166 --> 03:48.207
\Dante! Dante! Dante! Dante!

24
03:48.208 --> 03:50.791
\What on earth is going on there?

25
04:04.791 --> 04:07.415
- What was the question? - Were you partying last night?

26
04:07.416 --> 04:11.041
Pictures of you at Afterlife are making the rounds on social media.

27
04:12.625 --> 04:15.958
Impossible. Cameras aren't allowed in there.

28
04:17.583 --> 04:19.832
You think your performance is funny, too?

29
04:19.833 --> 04:22.457
Your escapades got you kicked out of Formula 1.

30
04:22.458 --> 04:24.290
- WHAT'S THE PLAN? - I'M GONNA END THIS!

31
04:24.291 --> 04:27.082
You're in third place after five Euro GT races.

32
04:27.083 --> 04:28.124
Last year, Ruben,

33
04:28.125 --> 04:31.624
who had been benched because of you, came in first place.

34
04:31.625 --> 04:35.415
The Lamont race is next week, but you're partying and letting yourself go.

35
04:35.416 --> 04:38.040
- You've done your research, huh? - Nothing but the facts.

36
04:38.041 --> 04:42.082
The fact is that within the team we may have different ideas about "how,"

37
04:42.083 --> 04:43.332
but not about "what."

38
04:43.333 --> 04:46.290
- And what is this "what"? - Winning the season, what else?

39
04:46.291 --> 04:48.040
And what if Dante doesn't win?

40
04:48.041 --> 04:52.041
As the team leader, aren't you already taking a big risk, given his problems?

41
04:56.166 --> 04:57.999
We have confidence in Dante.

42
04:58.000 --> 05:01.707
That's it. Thanks a lot, that's all. Have a great day, see you next time.

43
05:01.708 --> 05:03.041
Dante, one last question.

44
05:03.500 --> 05:06.665
It's been nearly two years since your sister's tragic accident.

45
05:06.666 --> 05:08.665
Would she be proud of your lifestyle?

46
05:08.666 --> 05:11.165
- What did you just say? - Honestly.

47
05:11.166 --> 05:12.540
- Okay. - You son of a bitch!

48
05:12.541 --> 05:13.707
- Hey! - That's too much!

49
05:13.708 --> 05:15.165
- Stop! - Get out!

50
05:15.166 --> 05:16.291
- What did you say? - Hey!

51
05:17.125 --> 05:18.332
Hey!

52
05:18.333 --> 05:20.874
No alcohol, no parties, no nothing!

53
05:20.875 --> 05:22.915
It's all in the contract, in black and white.

54
05:22.916 --> 05:25.582
Last night's pictures mean a 20,000 euro fine!

55
05:25.583 --> 05:27.707
And that stunt in there? Another 20.

56
05:27.708 --> 05:30.540
- I know my contract. - Then act like it.

57
05:30.541 --> 05:31.625
Okay, that's enough.

58
05:34.250 --> 05:35.791
Dante, you good?

59
05:36.333 --> 05:38.750
Or do you want Ruben to take over the training?

60
05:39.750 --> 05:40.583
Dream on.

61
05:41.166 --> 05:43.208
Go, get outta here, you three. Go train.

62
05:44.333 --> 05:45.375
Come on, let's go.

63
06:07.583 --> 06:09.707
289 kilometers per hour!

64
06:09.708 --> 06:12.625
Maybe we should set reporters on you more often, kid.

65
06:25.083 --> 06:26.750
That's a record!

66
06:27.166 --> 06:28.749
- Sweet! - Yes!

67
06:28.750 --> 06:31.833
I get that you're angry, Mr. Richter. I am, too.

68
06:34.708 --> 06:35.791
I understand.

69
06:41.916 --> 06:42.832
And?

70
06:42.833 --> 06:45.833
Our biggest sponsor is pulling out until further notice.

71
06:52.208 --> 06:53.916
Get ready for the pit stop.

72
06:55.166 --> 06:57.875
- You ready, Sarah? - Yeah, I'm ready.

73
07:05.833 --> 07:08.999
No way! Hey, Timo! Is this for real?

74
07:09.000 --> 07:11.708
- Man, bunch of amateurs here. - Wait, I have a spare part.

75
07:17.416 --> 07:20.582
Okay, folks. Nearly perfect doesn't win races.

76
07:20.583 --> 07:24.166
It would have been a great time had Timo not screwed up again. Thanks.

77
07:27.041 --> 07:29.832
You can thank the newbie.

78
07:29.833 --> 07:32.750
This is Sarah. She's the new mechanic on the team.

79
07:33.250 --> 07:35.624
- All right. So, from now on, total focus… - Thanks.

80
07:35.625 --> 07:37.125
…on the Lamont race!

81
07:37.708 --> 07:39.750
Your friends and families have been told!

82
07:40.291 --> 07:42.208
They won't be seeing you before Christmas.

83
07:55.916 --> 07:57.000
Sarah?

84
07:58.333 --> 07:59.499
Hey.

85
07:59.500 --> 08:00.458
Awesome.

86
08:01.208 --> 08:04.041
- It's been a long time. - Yeah. Hey.

87
08:05.291 --> 08:08.458
Yeah, Kids' Kart Racing, 2012.

88
08:10.333 --> 08:12.708
- "See you at the finish line!" - Yeah.

89
08:13.458 --> 08:15.541
Weren't you even faster than me one time?

90
08:16.375 --> 08:19.790
- One time? - Well, we'll see about that.

91
08:19.791 --> 08:21.750
So, how are you? Still driving?

92
08:23.083 --> 08:25.416
Only on the PlayStation.

93
08:26.583 --> 08:27.666
That makes two of us.

94
08:29.541 --> 08:31.499
Why didn't you say anything?

95
08:31.500 --> 08:33.583
I could've put in a good word for you.

96
08:35.041 --> 08:36.583
I wanted to do it by myself.

97
08:40.166 --> 08:41.166
Makes sense.

98
08:45.791 --> 08:46.875
How's your mom?

99
08:51.000 --> 08:52.083
Good.

100
08:55.000 --> 08:55.833
Good.

101
08:58.083 --> 08:59.083
Can you…

102
09:00.166 --> 09:01.957
Give her my best regards.

103
09:01.958 --> 09:04.375
Yeah, I will. See you.

104
09:05.708 --> 09:09.041
And… if you ever need someone to talk to…

105
09:10.416 --> 09:11.500
Any time.

106
10:11.083 --> 10:12.790
- You're Sarah, right? - Yes.

107
10:12.791 --> 10:15.583
I'm Tanya. I do press and marketing.

108
10:16.583 --> 10:18.208
- Nice to meet you. - Nice to meet you.

109
10:21.375 --> 10:22.499
Oh, no, not her.

110
10:22.500 --> 10:24.040
EVA MARIA FISCHER CELEBRITY EXPERT

111
10:24.041 --> 10:25.083
Oh, God.

112
10:26.833 --> 10:27.999
Note for tomorrow.

113
10:28.000 --> 10:31.875
Call Eva Maria Fischer's editors.

114
10:33.583 --> 10:35.291
Here's a little tip, by the way.

115
10:36.208 --> 10:39.499
Anyone who wants to get along with Dante,

116
10:39.500 --> 10:42.624
never talk to him about his sister.

117
10:42.625 --> 10:44.083
Never, ever.

118
10:44.833 --> 10:45.666
Yeah.

119
11:12.791 --> 11:14.041
This room's for everyone.

120
11:15.333 --> 11:16.833
You don't mind?

121
11:17.916 --> 11:18.750
No.

122
11:20.166 --> 11:21.250
It'd be weird anyway.

123
11:23.000 --> 11:24.541
You're part of the team, after all.

124
11:35.250 --> 11:36.083
Shit.

125
11:41.041 --> 11:43.583
- Hold still. - You got any scissors or something?

126
11:46.625 --> 11:47.458
Hold still.

127
11:51.333 --> 11:53.166
If you want to work for me,

128
11:54.875 --> 11:56.541
we have to trust each other blindly.

129
12:01.958 --> 12:02.791
Okay?

130
12:03.708 --> 12:04.750
Okay.

131
12:08.958 --> 12:10.833
If you ever need help,

132
12:12.583 --> 12:14.250
just let me know.

133
12:19.833 --> 12:20.875
See you, Sandra.

134
12:22.083 --> 12:23.041
Sarah.

135
12:37.833 --> 12:38.875
Mom?

136
13:04.833 --> 13:08.875
REGARDING: DEBTS DEAR MRS. JENKINS,

137
13:25.500 --> 13:27.708
KART RACING 1st PLACE

138
13:45.333 --> 13:48.375
I want to be a driver, too. Like you.

139
13:48.916 --> 13:51.041
\Once a driver, always a driver.

140
13:56.208 --> 13:58.665
\ESCALATED PRESS CONFERENCE TEAM EAGLE

141
13:58.666 --> 14:01.000
- What did you say? - Get out!

142
14:16.041 --> 14:18.457
How's Dante Annunziata doing?

143
14:18.458 --> 14:21.915
Not good, I tell you what. First, the crazy stories about his affairs,

144
14:21.916 --> 14:24.749
and then the excessive drinking and endless parties.

145
14:24.750 --> 14:27.874
No wonder he was kicked out of Formula 1 last year.

146
14:27.875 --> 14:30.499
Since the death of his sister, he seems totally lost.

147
14:30.500 --> 14:33.750
\It's a shame when you remember that he was right at the top.

148
14:45.958 --> 14:49.207
\Oh, my God, guys. Have you seen this photo?

149
14:49.208 --> 14:52.540
\I'm so totally shocked. What's going on with Dante Annunziata?

150
14:52.541 --> 14:53.666
I don't know who…

151
14:58.375 --> 14:59.791
\WHAT HAPPENED IN THE LOCKER ROOM?

152
15:03.958 --> 15:05.207
Whoa! Dante!

153
15:05.208 --> 15:06.791
I want to know all the details.

154
15:08.791 --> 15:13.290
\The racing star and the mechanic. A steamy workplace romance.

155
15:13.291 --> 15:15.333
\The sponsors are not happy at all.

156
15:18.750 --> 15:20.083
- What? - Fuck!

157
15:21.916 --> 15:23.708
I swear, nothing happened. It was nothing.

158
15:26.541 --> 15:27.665
Sarah.

159
15:27.666 --> 15:28.750
Not now, okay?

160
15:30.166 --> 15:33.124
This is a huge media scandal. The sponsors are going nuts.

161
15:33.125 --> 15:35.540
- You are suspended. - It's a misunderstanding.

162
15:35.541 --> 15:39.250
- I can explain. I don't know how… - It is what it is.

163
15:40.708 --> 15:43.707
- I have to let you go. - But nothing happened!

164
15:43.708 --> 15:45.166
I'm sorry.

165
15:57.958 --> 16:01.083
Richter will pull out as a sponsor if you continue to race with us.

166
16:04.000 --> 16:06.665
You're not just our driver, Dante.

167
16:06.666 --> 16:09.832
You're our face, too. A brand ambassador!

168
16:09.833 --> 16:14.333
And right now, you are an absolute disaster for the brand.

169
16:23.458 --> 16:25.083
You're not a good role model.

170
16:26.291 --> 16:28.416
I never was.

171
16:40.458 --> 16:41.833
Well, you're right.

172
16:42.666 --> 16:45.083
It's true. For us, it's not just about winning.

173
16:46.375 --> 16:47.625
We need a story.

174
16:48.583 --> 16:50.750
We need to tell people a story.

175
16:51.791 --> 16:53.333
What kind of story?

176
17:18.208 --> 17:19.250
Sarah?

177
17:27.750 --> 17:29.250
Are you lost?

178
17:30.666 --> 17:31.500
No.

179
17:41.416 --> 17:44.291
I think we have both had a pretty shitty day.

180
17:46.666 --> 17:48.125
I'm unemployed.

181
17:49.000 --> 17:53.000
You've got 600 horsepower under that hood. Your day can't be that shitty.

182
17:55.375 --> 17:58.625
Okay. Snappy, like your father.

183
18:01.916 --> 18:04.833
I knew him. From back when he was still racing.

184
18:05.541 --> 18:06.583
A huge talent.

185
18:09.250 --> 18:11.750
But without money, you can't go far in this sport.

186
18:14.458 --> 18:17.207
I know how much Tommy believed in you.

187
18:17.208 --> 18:20.916
That he went into debt financing your dream.

188
18:24.458 --> 18:28.041
My father wasn't cold in the ground before a letter came from the tax office.

189
18:29.000 --> 18:30.375
180,000 euros.

190
18:31.583 --> 18:34.250
That's been hanging over us ever since I was 16.

191
18:35.041 --> 18:36.500
You feel responsible.

192
18:39.833 --> 18:41.125
Why are you here?

193
18:46.750 --> 18:47.583
Test drive.

194
19:06.375 --> 19:08.958
You've got 600 horsepower under the hood.

195
19:10.208 --> 19:11.999
Not such a shitty day anymore, is it?

196
19:12.000 --> 19:16.374
If this is about me going public, don't worry, that's not who I am.

197
19:16.375 --> 19:18.666
- No, that's not it. - So what is this about?

198
19:19.333 --> 19:21.750
A deal that's good for everyone.

199
19:30.208 --> 19:33.208
In public, you play Dante's sweetheart until the end of the season.

200
19:34.375 --> 19:35.916
And in return…

201
19:37.250 --> 19:40.625
Sarah, wait. Sarah, wait a minute.

202
19:42.000 --> 19:43.583
I'll pay off your debt.

203
19:44.208 --> 19:46.875
All of it. The whole 180,000.

204
19:49.208 --> 19:50.416
And that's not all.

205
19:51.250 --> 19:52.750
You want to drive.

206
19:54.583 --> 19:56.166
I mean, really drive.

207
19:57.791 --> 20:00.207
I'm giving you the chance to be the first woman driver

208
20:00.208 --> 20:02.166
in the history of Eagle Racing.

209
20:03.625 --> 20:06.540
If Dante wins the season, he's back in Formula 1.

210
20:06.541 --> 20:09.500
If he loses, he's out. Either way, I need a new number one.

211
20:10.958 --> 20:12.875
Ruben? What about Ruben?

212
20:13.500 --> 20:15.041
Not if you're faster.

213
20:16.708 --> 20:19.624
I see what your father saw in you, Sarah.

214
20:19.625 --> 20:21.582
And I'm ready to invest.

215
20:21.583 --> 20:25.624
Play the role of Dante's girlfriend, and put this scandal to bed,

216
20:25.625 --> 20:29.166
and I'll get you the best training money can buy.

217
20:31.083 --> 20:32.750
But there is one condition.

218
20:34.208 --> 20:38.124
No one can know about our little agreement. No one.

219
20:38.125 --> 20:39.749
Certainly not Dante.

220
20:39.750 --> 20:42.624
He must not know about your training.

221
20:42.625 --> 20:44.958
He thinks this is his story.

222
20:47.041 --> 20:48.125
Make it yours.

223
20:49.375 --> 20:50.208
You hear me?

224
20:50.958 --> 20:52.083
Make it yours.

225
21:03.375 --> 21:06.124
"In return for this undertaking, Eagle Racing agrees,

226
21:06.125 --> 21:08.749
upon fulfilment, to provide the following."

227
21:08.750 --> 21:12.540
"First, a payment of 200,000 euros to Ms. Jenkins."

228
21:12.541 --> 21:13.874
As if that's believable.

229
21:13.875 --> 21:16.874
People will talk about it, and that's what matters.

230
21:16.875 --> 21:18.541
Manipulate, confuse and destroy.

231
21:19.875 --> 21:24.499
"Second, both parties agree to make their social media

232
21:24.500 --> 21:28.125
and other media appearances fully available, and

233
21:29.833 --> 21:33.416
to display affection in public as circumstances require."

234
21:34.041 --> 21:34.916
What?

235
21:36.375 --> 21:39.082
Holding hands, shopping arm in arm, that kind of thing.

236
21:39.083 --> 21:41.666
Kissing. We're talking about kissing, okay?

237
21:42.625 --> 21:44.375
Do we know if she's healthy?

238
21:46.208 --> 21:47.833
Sorry, who are you?

239
21:49.666 --> 21:50.875
His mother.

240
21:51.833 --> 21:54.624
Dante can't catch anything during the season.

241
21:54.625 --> 21:57.832
The guy who never sleeps with the same woman twice?

242
21:57.833 --> 21:58.666
Says who?

243
21:59.458 --> 22:00.582
The Internet.

244
22:00.583 --> 22:03.249
Tomorrow, the Internet will say that I love you.

245
22:03.250 --> 22:04.250
Go on, please.

246
22:05.541 --> 22:09.707
"Emphasized here in particular as an explicit stipulation of the contract,

247
22:09.708 --> 22:14.083
a kiss on the red carpet at the European Sports Awards in Monaco."

248
22:15.041 --> 22:18.457
"This contract is strictly confidential."

249
22:18.458 --> 22:21.499
It doesn't say that there are no other verbal agreements.

250
22:21.500 --> 22:23.333
Normally, that's standard, isn't it?

251
22:25.208 --> 22:27.290
No problem. Consider it agreed.

252
22:27.291 --> 22:28.208
Good.

253
22:44.666 --> 22:47.416
You don't touch me without my permission.

254
22:47.916 --> 22:49.500
It'll be my pleasure.

255
22:53.541 --> 22:55.624
Where did we meet?

256
22:55.625 --> 22:56.624
Good question!

257
22:56.625 --> 23:01.624
It wasn't just love at first sight, but a savior in a moment of need.

258
23:01.625 --> 23:05.540
An eye-wateringly expensive restaurant high above the city skyline.

259
23:05.541 --> 23:07.916
You saw her and reacted at once.

260
23:08.750 --> 23:09.708
Are you all right?

261
23:10.708 --> 23:13.750
- Isn't that a bit much? - So she should have choked?

262
23:16.791 --> 23:19.124
- Of course not. - So, anyway…

263
23:19.125 --> 23:23.790
In that moment, there was a spark. Love at first sight.

264
23:23.791 --> 23:24.749
Thank you.

265
23:24.750 --> 23:27.541
But it was a false start. They didn't exchange numbers.

266
23:28.208 --> 23:31.957
Tough situation. But destiny doesn't give up that easily,

267
23:31.958 --> 23:34.166
and so it shifted things up a gear.

268
23:34.750 --> 23:38.083
It was Sarah's first day at Team Eagle and whoosh!

269
23:42.208 --> 23:45.749
Suddenly, you see each other again, and the world stands still.

270
23:45.750 --> 23:49.290
Meaningful glances, racing pulses, the works.

271
23:49.291 --> 23:51.374
Just like in the movies.

272
23:51.375 --> 23:53.583
From then on, you really hit the gas.

273
23:54.916 --> 23:57.916
Love in the fast lane, and in pole position.

274
23:58.625 --> 24:00.665
And today is the big day.

275
24:00.666 --> 24:04.999
The day that a video of you going shopping for rings will go viral.

276
24:05.000 --> 24:09.457
Not just any ring. White gold, 15 karat, at least.

277
24:09.458 --> 24:12.124
Sarah has no idea, of course,

278
24:12.125 --> 24:15.707
as she heads back to the place where it all began.

279
24:15.708 --> 24:16.625
That's good.

280
24:18.375 --> 24:19.250
Yeah.

281
24:36.500 --> 24:37.625
You're drooling.

282
24:42.250 --> 24:43.624
I can't do this.

283
24:43.625 --> 24:46.041
I imagine that women hear that from you pretty often.

284
24:47.750 --> 24:50.125
Pretty dry. I bet there's sand in your gearbox.

285
24:53.666 --> 24:56.083
Thanks. I needed that.

286
25:02.750 --> 25:03.791
What are you doing?

287
25:04.500 --> 25:06.291
Making the biggest mistake of my life.

288
25:10.000 --> 25:12.125
Will you marry me?

289
25:14.791 --> 25:15.750
Of course.

290
25:21.750 --> 25:24.708
- Did you pick it out all by yourself? - Shut up.

291
25:25.541 --> 25:29.249
It now turns out that racing driver Dante Annunziata

292
25:29.250 --> 25:33.624
\is driving in the fast lane, heading for pole position.

293
25:33.625 --> 25:38.165
From major scandal to great love.

294
25:38.166 --> 25:41.583
- You're a PR genius. - Oh, God. Eva Maria Fischer, thank you.

295
25:42.625 --> 25:43.874
Oh, God.

296
25:43.875 --> 25:47.915
I understand that you're overwhelmed. I am, too, but…

297
25:47.916 --> 25:50.499
It's not what everyone thinks. He's…

298
25:50.500 --> 25:53.999
He's charming and funny, and…

299
25:54.000 --> 25:56.457
He has such beautiful eyes.

300
25:56.458 --> 26:01.041
He smells really good. He's a catch.

301
26:04.333 --> 26:05.583
Look at me.

302
26:06.416 --> 26:08.041
Something's not right here.

303
26:08.625 --> 26:11.332
You've never even mentioned this guy.

304
26:11.333 --> 26:13.833
And all of sudden, you're engaged?

305
26:15.333 --> 26:16.916
And you're flying to Monaco?

306
26:19.750 --> 26:21.500
You're hiding something from me.

307
26:25.750 --> 26:27.541
Promise me you'll keep this a secret?

308
26:29.375 --> 26:30.291
Okay.

309
26:31.500 --> 26:34.333
Our debts are about to go away forever. Here.

310
26:36.625 --> 26:37.750
\In black and white.

311
26:38.458 --> 26:40.874
\Mom, they're paying us 200,000 euros.

312
26:40.875 --> 26:45.333
\And all I have to do is pretend to be engaged to an idiot.

313
26:48.625 --> 26:50.083
- Sweetie… - Mom, please.

314
26:51.541 --> 26:53.041
I can do this.

315
27:24.166 --> 27:26.749
So, little update on tonight's gala.

316
27:26.750 --> 27:28.499
Pickup is at 8:00 p.m.

317
27:28.500 --> 27:29.832
On the dot. Downstairs.

318
27:29.833 --> 27:35.124
The makeup artist figures you'll be done in two-and-a-half, three hours.

319
27:35.125 --> 27:36.124
Three hours?

320
27:36.125 --> 27:37.625
- Yeah. - If that's all it takes.

321
27:38.875 --> 27:40.124
That's mean.

322
27:40.125 --> 27:42.957
So, don't worry about a thing.

323
27:42.958 --> 27:45.666
I know you're gonna look amazing. Okay?

324
27:46.208 --> 27:49.790
And in terms of styling, you've got a few options ready, right?

325
27:49.791 --> 27:51.082
You mean clothes?

326
27:51.083 --> 27:53.832
I mean evening gowns. So, yes, clothes.

327
27:53.833 --> 27:57.582
This was all in the email that I expect you've read.

328
27:57.583 --> 27:59.707
Yes. Yes.

329
27:59.708 --> 28:03.790
Perfect, my fiancée is walking down the red carpet in gym clothes.

330
28:03.791 --> 28:07.249
Better than your models in their see-through outfits!

331
28:07.250 --> 28:08.791
They have nothing to hide, is all.

332
28:10.208 --> 28:12.375
Is that why you're not wearing see-through pants?

333
28:14.750 --> 28:15.583
Touché.

334
28:41.750 --> 28:44.665
Welcome back, Signore Annunziata.

335
28:44.666 --> 28:46.957
It's always a pleasure to see you.

336
28:46.958 --> 28:49.040
The pleasure is all mine.

337
28:49.041 --> 28:51.541
The same room as last time?

338
28:55.833 --> 28:59.958
Oh, the honeymoon suite has been booked for you.

339
29:02.958 --> 29:08.207
That's what it says in the system. For Mr. Annunziata and Ms. Jenkins.

340
29:08.208 --> 29:11.707
- Jenkins. - Ms. Jenkins.

341
29:11.708 --> 29:12.708
Jenkins.

342
29:14.958 --> 29:17.833
This is all a little new for both of us.

343
29:18.500 --> 29:19.458
Right.

344
29:20.041 --> 29:20.875
Come along.

345
29:26.833 --> 29:30.457
Fuck whoever you want, but you're getting your own room.

346
29:30.458 --> 29:32.500
- You jealous? - No.

347
29:33.083 --> 29:36.000
Just struck by how consistent you are about trophy hunting.

348
29:36.916 --> 29:39.500
Unlike you, I get paid for it.

349
29:42.875 --> 29:45.374
I hear you used to race, too?

350
29:45.375 --> 29:47.541
German Junior Kart Champion 2014.

351
29:48.166 --> 29:49.833
Once a driver, always a driver.

352
29:50.500 --> 29:52.750
That's what people who aren't drivers anymore say.

353
29:53.708 --> 29:55.041
If you say so.

354
30:17.250 --> 30:20.290
You take the bedroom. I'll take the couch. No problem.

355
30:20.291 --> 30:21.375
Strawberry?

356
30:27.791 --> 30:29.290
I only like white chocolate.

357
30:29.291 --> 30:31.207
- That's not chocolate. - Question of taste.

358
30:31.208 --> 30:32.333
Question of character.

359
30:34.500 --> 30:36.958
I'm just not the bitter type.

360
30:45.958 --> 30:50.165
Hi, it's Tanya again. Send me a couple of outfit options for tonight.

361
30:50.166 --> 30:51.749
- Thanks, kiss kiss. - Shit.

362
30:51.750 --> 30:52.832
When's your flight?

363
30:52.833 --> 30:54.665
Mom, we arrived today.

364
30:54.666 --> 30:56.082
- Not tomorrow? - No.

365
30:56.083 --> 30:57.500
Then I can't come with you.

366
31:18.625 --> 31:19.666
Hello?

367
31:36.916 --> 31:38.333
Can I help you?

368
31:40.166 --> 31:41.750
I think I'm in the wrong place.

369
31:43.541 --> 31:46.124
Sarah… Sarah Jenkins!

370
31:46.125 --> 31:47.958
You're in the right place. Welcome.

371
31:48.791 --> 31:50.082
How do you know me?

372
31:50.083 --> 31:53.874
Everyone knows Dante Annunziata's fiancée. Hello?

373
31:53.875 --> 31:55.957
He has a really good eye.

374
31:55.958 --> 31:59.249
Being honest? When I saw you from behind, I thought,

375
31:59.250 --> 32:01.249
"Security! Get this hobo outta here!"

376
32:01.250 --> 32:03.332
But, my God, you're pretty. Unbelievable!

377
32:03.333 --> 32:05.625
Looking for something for the awards show tonight?

378
32:07.583 --> 32:08.458
Yes.

379
32:11.541 --> 32:13.375
Okay, this could work, right?

380
32:13.958 --> 32:15.290
No, too big.

381
32:15.291 --> 32:18.207
You could wear this as a parachute, but not to the gala.

382
32:18.208 --> 32:19.416
We'll find something.

383
32:21.583 --> 32:23.874
You look a little bit like E.T.

384
32:23.875 --> 32:26.582
- Like a ball bearing. - Or a conspiracy theorist.

385
32:26.583 --> 32:28.707
I like the yellow one.

386
32:28.708 --> 32:30.125
No, that's too… too basic.

387
32:32.166 --> 32:34.291
Oh, that's also really, really nice.

388
32:56.041 --> 32:58.041
I think it's… too much.

389
32:58.791 --> 32:59.958
It's beautiful.

390
33:00.708 --> 33:02.291
I prefer the black one.

391
33:03.041 --> 33:04.541
That one's beautiful too.

392
33:11.083 --> 33:14.291
- So, that'll be… - Perfect timing!

393
33:17.416 --> 33:19.416
Guess you didn't have anything on you?

394
33:20.875 --> 33:24.707
That will be 6,600 euros.

395
33:24.708 --> 33:27.582
- What? - And the sparkly dress too, please.

396
33:27.583 --> 33:28.416
Okay.

397
33:36.583 --> 33:37.750
You were watching me.

398
33:39.791 --> 33:41.250
You like the thought of that?

399
33:49.208 --> 33:51.250
Your makeup artist is waiting for you.

400
34:54.666 --> 34:55.500
Hey.

401
35:00.250 --> 35:01.957
Do I look halfway decent?

402
35:01.958 --> 35:06.333
"Halfway decent" would be the understatement of the year.

403
35:09.125 --> 35:10.999
It only took three hours, after all.

404
35:11.000 --> 35:13.416
I can't leave you alone for a moment.

405
35:16.166 --> 35:17.708
And how could I?

406
35:22.458 --> 35:24.958
Hey, spare. How was your flight?

407
35:27.083 --> 35:28.750
Not great, I gotta say.

408
35:29.333 --> 35:31.082
Like your sense of humor.

409
35:31.083 --> 35:32.915
Hey, hey. There you are!

410
35:32.916 --> 35:37.333
Wow, you three look great. Time to get going. The shuttle's here.

411
35:50.541 --> 35:51.708
You two ever have a thing?

412
35:53.708 --> 35:54.833
Who?

413
35:57.250 --> 35:58.083
You and Ruben?

414
35:58.750 --> 35:59.874
No.

415
35:59.875 --> 36:02.375
We were in the same karting school.

416
36:06.875 --> 36:08.166
Jealous?

417
36:09.958 --> 36:11.125
It's just a job.

418
36:12.791 --> 36:14.250
No more, no less.

419
36:59.083 --> 37:00.083
Everything okay?

420
37:05.833 --> 37:06.833
Kiss!

421
37:08.041 --> 37:09.915
- Look at the camera. - This way, everyone!

422
37:09.916 --> 37:10.958
Can you kiss now?

423
37:12.666 --> 37:14.583
It's just a job, right?

424
37:17.458 --> 37:18.541
It's all fake.

425
37:19.250 --> 37:20.375
It's all fake.

426
38:12.791 --> 38:16.040
And welcome to this year's European Sports Awards,

427
38:16.041 --> 38:17.082
live from Monaco.

428
38:17.083 --> 38:20.124
My name is Steven Gätjen, and this is the first highlight

429
38:20.125 --> 38:21.915
from today's awards ceremony.

430
38:21.916 --> 38:23.540
Here's Dante Annunziata.

431
38:23.541 --> 38:27.165
No trophy this time, but with Sarah and a kiss

432
38:27.166 --> 38:30.499
that will have hearts racing on the red carpet.

433
38:30.500 --> 38:32.583
That is true love.

434
38:48.000 --> 38:50.875
- Mr. Richter! - Here they come.

435
38:51.416 --> 38:52.583
Our dream couple.

436
38:55.583 --> 38:58.665
Even better looking in the flesh than in pictures.

437
38:58.666 --> 39:01.082
- It's a pleasure to meet you. - Likewise.

438
39:01.083 --> 39:03.749
It's great that he was able to score you so quickly,

439
39:03.750 --> 39:06.416
but I'd prefer a win at Lamont.

440
39:08.041 --> 39:09.208
We're working on it.

441
39:10.041 --> 39:14.416
I see from the papers that you've put his little fire out?

442
39:15.041 --> 39:15.958
Have I?

443
39:16.958 --> 39:20.500
Sarah has helped me discover a new side of myself.

444
39:21.458 --> 39:23.333
The main thing is to not get any slower.

445
39:28.458 --> 39:31.124
You bear a striking resemblance to your sister.

446
39:31.125 --> 39:33.458
You really are her spitting image.

447
39:35.833 --> 39:37.000
Did you know Gabriella?

448
39:38.833 --> 39:40.582
Personally? No.

449
39:40.583 --> 39:46.333
But I understand she was a very talented driver.

450
39:47.625 --> 39:50.041
Excuse me. Come along, I want to dance.

451
39:51.416 --> 39:52.250
Thank you.

452
39:54.291 --> 39:55.624
What an asshole.

453
39:55.625 --> 39:58.582
How dare he provoke you like that!

454
39:58.583 --> 39:59.583
Hey.

455
40:00.791 --> 40:03.125
You look really beautiful in that dress.

456
40:05.541 --> 40:07.916
And it's not even see-through.

457
40:16.416 --> 40:18.000
Did you wear it for me?

458
40:21.125 --> 40:22.458
Maybe.

459
40:27.500 --> 40:30.208
But don't expect me to take it off for you.

460
40:37.541 --> 40:39.750
Aren't they sweet?

461
40:41.166 --> 40:43.041
Almost too good to be true.

462
40:43.750 --> 40:46.125
Some people are saying that it's all a hoax.

463
40:49.583 --> 40:50.416
Who?

464
40:52.625 --> 40:55.665
…who took pictures of Dante and Sarah shopping.

465
40:55.666 --> 40:59.625
It doesn't look like they're in love. Is this all fake?

466
41:01.791 --> 41:05.875
I think that looks pretty authentic, if you ask my opinion.

467
41:37.750 --> 41:40.083
You can stop, no one can see us here.

468
41:40.666 --> 41:42.125
What if I don't want to?

469
42:33.541 --> 42:34.666
Good morning. Sleep well?

470
42:35.625 --> 42:38.249
- Yes. - Your kiss yesterday, that was…

471
42:38.250 --> 42:42.375
It was a convincing performance. Excellent work. Check, please.

472
42:44.375 --> 42:45.375
You're welcome.

473
42:45.916 --> 42:49.541
So, our deal stands. Training starts after Lamont.

474
42:53.541 --> 42:55.541
- Are you still there? - Yeah, yeah.

475
42:57.041 --> 42:58.915
I'm still here. I…

476
42:58.916 --> 43:02.541
- I'm looking forward to it. - Remember, not a word to Dante.

477
43:28.041 --> 43:32.375
I think I'm clearly the cuter of us two.

478
43:38.250 --> 43:41.833
Interesting experience, to be the one waking up alone.

479
43:48.208 --> 43:50.416
There's a first time for everything.

480
43:57.833 --> 44:02.875
Do you want to tell me that last night was a mistake?

481
44:04.500 --> 44:08.083
That everything should stay strictly business between us?

482
44:12.666 --> 44:14.250
Exactly.

483
44:16.000 --> 44:17.166
I'm sorry.

484
44:32.375 --> 44:37.208
The Grand Prix of Lamont, with its traditionally unpredictable weather.

485
44:38.875 --> 44:41.415
Here and now, absolutely anything could happen.

486
44:41.416 --> 44:43.750
It's an important date in the Euro Masters calendar.

487
44:46.291 --> 44:48.290
Tough conditions again today.

488
44:48.291 --> 44:51.332
The fans have a really exciting race to look forward to,

489
44:51.333 --> 44:54.125
but for the teams, this will be a test of their courage.

490
45:15.166 --> 45:17.500
It won't be an easy day for him.

491
45:19.041 --> 45:20.250
Why not?

492
45:22.083 --> 45:24.083
It's his sister's birthday.

493
45:26.375 --> 45:28.541
Today of all days.

494
45:35.541 --> 45:38.000
Hey, take care of yourself, Sarah.

495
45:39.500 --> 45:40.582
What do you mean?

496
45:40.583 --> 45:44.375
What do I mean? I can see you have feelings for him.

497
45:47.250 --> 45:48.083
Nonsense!

498
45:49.375 --> 45:51.665
Bronson told me about your little deal.

499
45:51.666 --> 45:54.583
You've got big plans. Don't forget that.

500
46:02.000 --> 46:04.249
And now it's almost time.

501
46:04.250 --> 46:08.374
A few seconds from the start. The Grand Prix of Lamont.

502
46:08.375 --> 46:11.582
Annunziata is starting in fifth place, after a tough qualifying session,

503
46:11.583 --> 46:16.707
and he'll need a minor miracle today if he wants a shot at the championship.

504
46:16.708 --> 46:19.208
Second place, at least. No easy task.

505
46:23.625 --> 46:24.958
Come on.

506
46:38.666 --> 46:41.790
Very good start from Annunziata, off to a flying start in this race.

507
46:41.791 --> 46:43.083
Good performance.

508
46:46.125 --> 46:49.540
Annunziata is in top form, masterfully overtaking McKinnen here.

509
46:49.541 --> 46:51.916
In third place now. Who saw this coming?

510
46:52.916 --> 46:56.875
Ninth lap. The three drivers around Annunziata are neck-and-neck.

511
46:59.583 --> 47:03.374
This kind of supremacy on the racetrack is the reason he was signed.

512
47:03.375 --> 47:06.208
Dante Annunziata is really delivering today.

513
47:07.375 --> 47:11.749
And there it is, Annunziata takes the lead on the 16th lap, against all odds.

514
47:11.750 --> 47:12.790
Unbelievable.

515
47:12.791 --> 47:13.750
Yes!

516
47:25.875 --> 47:28.957
I've got… I've got a problem with the gear shift.

517
47:28.958 --> 47:30.666
Okay.

518
47:31.833 --> 47:33.374
Everything looks good on my end.

519
47:33.375 --> 47:36.875
Last lap at Lamont. Will Annunziata close it out today?

520
47:44.875 --> 47:46.249
What's he doing?

521
47:46.250 --> 47:50.082
No, Annunziata throws away victory, so close to the finish line.

522
47:50.083 --> 47:51.416
Second place.

523
47:52.083 --> 47:55.083
His nerves got the better of him. That's really tough.

524
48:25.375 --> 48:26.291
Hey!

525
48:28.291 --> 48:31.041
It was a good race. Second place.

526
48:40.833 --> 48:44.666
I… I know I shouldn't mention it, but I…

527
48:45.833 --> 48:48.208
- I think I know why you… - Please.

528
48:49.125 --> 48:50.999
Spare me the clever advice, okay?

529
48:51.000 --> 48:53.540
Believe me, you know nothing about me.

530
48:53.541 --> 48:55.915
You don't win races with your head.

531
48:55.916 --> 48:57.874
- You win with your heart. - Your heart?

532
48:57.875 --> 49:00.125
Is that your secret to success?

533
49:00.791 --> 49:02.583
Junior Kart Champ 2014?

534
49:04.125 --> 49:07.332
I'll let you in on a secret. You're not a driver.

535
49:07.333 --> 49:09.875
You never were, and you never will be.

536
49:16.416 --> 49:18.583
- Are you okay? - Leave me alone.

537
49:46.958 --> 49:49.208
Don't let anyone tell you what you aren't.

538
50:02.041 --> 50:02.958
Promise?

539
50:45.000 --> 50:48.040
Sorry, people, but this whole thing about being fake or not?

540
50:48.041 --> 50:50.790
Just look at this fucking kiss!

541
50:50.791 --> 50:54.124
Everyone who's ever been kissed like that knows that it's for real.

542
50:54.125 --> 50:55.333
So shut up.

543
50:59.333 --> 51:04.750
Sarah Jenkins hey sorry about

544
51:08.625 --> 51:14.875
I'm sorry about

545
51:17.791 --> 51:20.583
yo what's up

546
51:27.166 --> 51:29.457
Fits like a glove.

547
51:29.458 --> 51:31.666
- Can you hear me? - Loud and clear.

548
51:32.625 --> 51:34.000
And are you excited?

549
51:34.875 --> 51:35.708
Yes.

550
51:37.791 --> 51:38.958
You can do it.

551
51:42.958 --> 51:45.708
All right. Let's see if all this secrecy…

552
51:48.625 --> 51:50.416
I get it, you can drive.

553
51:53.500 --> 51:54.708
Not bad, Sarah.

554
51:56.583 --> 52:00.124
- Not bad at all. - For a woman, you mean?

555
52:00.125 --> 52:01.958
No, I'm not like that.

556
52:16.000 --> 52:19.750
\Hey, great training, Sarah. Keep it up. Pretty impress…

557
52:32.750 --> 52:34.125
Hey…

558
52:35.791 --> 52:37.833
I shouldn't have said that.

559
52:41.250 --> 52:42.416
I'm sorry.

560
52:47.083 --> 52:48.000
Good morning.

561
52:49.916 --> 52:52.458
So, quick briefing for you two.

562
52:54.958 --> 52:59.625
Nothing dramatic. No reason to panic. But we need to change course.

563
53:00.208 --> 53:03.332
Okay, people. My brother worked in the restaurant

564
53:03.333 --> 53:07.290
where Dante Annunziata is supposed to have saved Sarah's life.

565
53:07.291 --> 53:10.540
Strangely, my brother says that absolutely nobody saw it happen.

566
53:10.541 --> 53:11.375
Nobody.

567
53:13.875 --> 53:14.999
Yeah.

568
53:15.000 --> 53:18.040
It hasn't gotten far yet, but we need content.

569
53:18.041 --> 53:22.124
And good content. So look sharp.

570
53:22.125 --> 53:24.583
I've thought of something for tonight.

571
53:25.333 --> 53:26.708
Something real.

572
53:28.791 --> 53:29.875
I don't believe it.

573
53:30.708 --> 53:32.415
Back to the roots.

574
53:32.416 --> 53:34.957
- Good idea from Tanya. - I hear you.

575
53:34.958 --> 53:37.457
Yeah, but you don't stand a chance against me.

576
53:37.458 --> 53:39.500
- Oh, yeah? - I know.

577
53:50.625 --> 53:52.625
This is great. It still smells the same.

578
53:54.416 --> 53:59.625
Of burnt-out clutch and adolescent delusions of grandeur.

579
54:04.500 --> 54:07.582
Yeah, and of the rancid snack machine back there.

580
54:07.583 --> 54:12.375
We had one of those too, but it never had gummy bears.

581
54:35.208 --> 54:36.208
Is that you?

582
54:37.083 --> 54:37.916
Yeah.

583
54:38.958 --> 54:40.083
With my dad.

584
54:41.625 --> 54:42.625
And who's that?

585
54:44.958 --> 54:46.875
- That's Ruben. - What?

586
54:47.458 --> 54:49.750
- What? - Yeah.

587
54:50.291 --> 54:52.958
He was a little huskier back then.

588
54:59.208 --> 55:01.750
Your father's eyes are shining.

589
55:03.208 --> 55:04.291
Yeah.

590
55:08.541 --> 55:10.291
Dad was my hero.

591
55:13.625 --> 55:15.416
He always supported me.

592
55:17.041 --> 55:19.583
He's the reason I ever got involved in driving.

593
55:23.166 --> 55:25.624
When I was 16, he said,

594
55:25.625 --> 55:28.041
"Sarah, no more half measures now."

595
55:29.416 --> 55:31.874
And he bought me a brand-new kart.

596
55:31.875 --> 55:35.500
With a water-cooled two-stroke engine! And he found me a real coach.

597
55:37.791 --> 55:39.000
The works.

598
55:42.458 --> 55:44.666
Six months later, he died.

599
55:46.500 --> 55:47.791
Heart attack.

600
55:50.833 --> 55:52.415
That was when we found out

601
55:52.416 --> 55:55.500
that he'd got himself in debt so that I could drive.

602
55:57.833 --> 55:58.833
I'm sorry.

603
56:06.916 --> 56:08.208
You miss her.

604
56:12.208 --> 56:13.041
Every day.

605
56:36.416 --> 56:39.708
I think Tanya has written us a different story today.

606
56:58.291 --> 57:00.333
- You sabotaged my kart. - What?

607
57:03.541 --> 57:05.833
- You're doping. - I'm doping?

608
57:06.833 --> 57:09.625
I'm so clearly winning there.

609
57:13.208 --> 57:14.666
Let's go!

610
57:39.208 --> 57:40.999
That was a lot of fun.

611
57:41.000 --> 57:43.916
Yeah, I thought so too.

612
57:48.416 --> 57:50.500
Do you maybe want to go get a drink?

613
57:53.000 --> 57:54.457
Yeah.

614
57:54.458 --> 57:57.541
Jack - I'm waiting at the racetrack! Where are you?

615
58:03.750 --> 58:05.416
I gotta go home.

616
58:10.000 --> 58:12.874
No problem. Another time.

617
58:12.875 --> 58:14.416
Yeah, sorry.

618
58:21.166 --> 58:22.707
Sorry, Jack!

619
58:22.708 --> 58:24.290
I was with Dante.

620
58:24.291 --> 58:25.624
It won't happen again.

621
58:25.625 --> 58:28.332
Next time, step on the gas a little more.

622
58:28.333 --> 58:29.166
Yeah.

623
58:31.791 --> 58:33.291
You can strap yourself in.

624
58:34.250 --> 58:35.375
As punishment.

625
58:45.000 --> 58:48.624
I want to be a driver, too. Like you.

626
58:48.625 --> 58:51.041
Once a driver, always a driver.

627
59:39.708 --> 59:42.000
- You just beat the best time. - What?

628
59:43.000 --> 59:44.291
Dante's record.

629
59:47.666 --> 59:51.041
That's a new record for the track. This is incredible, Sarah.

630
01:00:12.291 --> 01:00:13.833
This woman works so hard.

631
01:00:15.250 --> 01:00:17.083
- Hey. - Hey.

632
01:00:19.833 --> 01:00:22.208
Hey, do you know if Dante was here last night?

633
01:00:25.250 --> 01:00:26.790
No idea, why?

634
01:00:26.791 --> 01:00:29.749
The guys are saying there's a new record in the system.

635
01:00:29.750 --> 01:00:30.958
And I didn't do it.

636
01:00:34.416 --> 01:00:36.416
Could be an error.

637
01:00:40.833 --> 01:00:41.833
Yeah.

638
01:00:42.583 --> 01:00:45.541
- I've gotta go shower. - Okay.

639
01:00:50.958 --> 01:00:53.957
After a truly stellar qualifying session yesterday,

640
01:00:53.958 --> 01:00:57.165
Annunziata could become a nightmare for the competition

641
01:00:57.166 --> 01:00:59.958
on the Alpen Racetrack today.

642
01:01:05.416 --> 01:01:07.124
But of course,

643
01:01:07.125 --> 01:01:10.124
the winner is just as easy to predict as the weather around here.

644
01:01:10.125 --> 01:01:11.374
That is, not at all.

645
01:01:11.375 --> 01:01:14.333
When it comes to slippery tracks, McKinnen is the expert.

646
01:01:20.000 --> 01:01:20.875
Thanks.

647
01:01:24.708 --> 01:01:25.541
Thank you.

648
01:01:30.125 --> 01:01:33.166
MOM

649
01:01:35.583 --> 01:01:36.625
Hey.

650
01:01:38.000 --> 01:01:38.833
Hi.

651
01:01:43.041 --> 01:01:45.707
Getting a chance is one thing.

652
01:01:45.708 --> 01:01:49.040
But very few people ever make use of it.

653
01:01:49.041 --> 01:01:51.916
Welcome to next year's shortlist.

654
01:01:53.041 --> 01:01:55.250
You should be proud of yourself, Sarah.

655
01:01:57.291 --> 01:01:58.250
Thanks.

656
01:02:01.375 --> 01:02:05.500
Sensational performance from Annunziata. Confidently overtaking here.

657
01:02:14.041 --> 01:02:15.250
Yes!

658
01:02:19.750 --> 01:02:20.750
Hi.

659
01:02:22.500 --> 01:02:23.458
Good luck.

660
01:02:25.208 --> 01:02:26.041
Thanks.

661
01:02:36.750 --> 01:02:39.165
All three are giving it their all today.

662
01:02:39.166 --> 01:02:42.749
McKinnen, Paulsen and Annunziata, they are all sensational.

663
01:02:42.750 --> 01:02:43.875
Who will hold his nerve?

664
01:02:45.791 --> 01:02:46.958
Will he do it?

665
01:02:50.541 --> 01:02:52.207
Will he? Will he?

666
01:02:52.208 --> 01:02:56.790
He overtakes. He's done it. Annunziata wins on the Alpen Racetrack.

667
01:02:56.791 --> 01:02:59.750
Sensational! What a finish!

668
01:03:09.708 --> 01:03:13.249
And this year's Alpen Racetrack champion,

669
01:03:13.250 --> 01:03:17.958
Dante Annunziata.

670
01:03:43.208 --> 01:03:45.500
Candidate driver?

671
01:03:48.458 --> 01:03:49.875
For next year?

672
01:03:54.583 --> 01:03:55.416
Mom,

673
01:03:56.416 --> 01:03:59.375
Mr. Bronson is serious about this. I'm sure of it.

674
01:04:00.166 --> 01:04:02.207
That, or he's using you.

675
01:04:02.208 --> 01:04:04.166
Or he's supporting me.

676
01:04:04.708 --> 01:04:06.875
Why haven't you told me anything about this?

677
01:04:09.541 --> 01:04:10.958
And what does Dante say?

678
01:04:17.541 --> 01:04:18.958
He doesn't know?

679
01:04:24.333 --> 01:04:27.457
Sweetheart, I can see that you have feelings for him.

680
01:04:27.458 --> 01:04:29.458
You have to talk to him.

681
01:04:34.416 --> 01:04:35.583
I'll get it.

682
01:04:46.291 --> 01:04:47.125
Hi.

683
01:04:51.000 --> 01:04:52.333
What are you doing here?

684
01:04:59.541 --> 01:05:00.541
Irene, right?

685
01:05:01.291 --> 01:05:02.125
Yes?

686
01:05:03.000 --> 01:05:04.458
Dante. It's nice to meet you.

687
01:05:10.958 --> 01:05:13.958
I wanted to… whisk you away.

688
01:05:19.541 --> 01:05:20.958
What if I don't want to go?

689
01:05:25.250 --> 01:05:27.333
Then it'll be a case for Interpol.

690
01:05:32.041 --> 01:05:36.125
We have almost exactly 68 hours before the dinner with the sponsors.

691
01:05:37.833 --> 01:05:39.083
We should be okay.

692
01:06:07.875 --> 01:06:08.958
Can we…

693
01:07:54.666 --> 01:07:57.916
I'd like to show you something I've never shown anyone before.

694
01:08:01.541 --> 01:08:02.375
Okay.

695
01:08:11.208 --> 01:08:12.832
The day the accident happened,

696
01:08:12.833 --> 01:08:15.415
we weren't just out for a drive, like everyone says.

697
01:08:15.416 --> 01:08:17.166
We were fighting.

698
01:08:18.583 --> 01:08:22.083
\Because I thought that she wasn't ready to go professional.

699
01:08:42.250 --> 01:08:44.208
I gave her this for her 18th birthday.

700
01:08:47.416 --> 01:08:49.583
"My angel with the bloody knees."

701
01:08:52.791 --> 01:08:54.375
That's what Mom always called her.

702
01:09:06.250 --> 01:09:08.582
Gabriella was very ambitious.

703
01:09:08.583 --> 01:09:10.333
A talented driver.

704
01:09:12.625 --> 01:09:14.000
Just like you.

705
01:09:17.291 --> 01:09:18.875
I didn't believe in her.

706
01:09:19.916 --> 01:09:21.291
I kept her small.

707
01:09:22.625 --> 01:09:26.875
And that's what set her off when she was next to me at the wheel.

708
01:09:29.208 --> 01:09:31.083
I'll never forget the way she looked at me.

709
01:09:36.541 --> 01:09:38.124
She drove off in a frenzy.

710
01:09:38.125 --> 01:09:40.415
She wanted to prove herself.

711
01:09:40.416 --> 01:09:41.625
And then, one mistake.

712
01:09:45.500 --> 01:09:48.750
She loses control of her car and dies instantly.

713
01:09:50.166 --> 01:09:51.208
Because of me.

714
01:10:10.000 --> 01:10:11.625
It's not your fault.

715
01:10:49.791 --> 01:10:51.916
- Morning. - Hey.

716
01:11:16.625 --> 01:11:19.708
What if we just ran away, when the season's over?

717
01:11:23.958 --> 01:11:25.125
Where?

718
01:11:26.083 --> 01:11:27.291
No idea.

719
01:11:28.916 --> 01:11:31.000
A fair in southern Italy.

720
01:11:36.041 --> 01:11:36.875
You and me…

721
01:11:39.666 --> 01:11:40.500
we could run

722
01:11:43.458 --> 01:11:45.791
a bumper car stand.

723
01:11:46.500 --> 01:11:48.000
That sounds nice.

724
01:12:55.583 --> 01:12:56.875
Do we really have to go?

725
01:12:59.416 --> 01:13:01.750
We have a contract. Or did you forget?

726
01:13:02.791 --> 01:13:04.666
In two days, it'll all be over.

727
01:13:08.375 --> 01:13:09.375
Yeah.

728
01:13:15.083 --> 01:13:16.416
Dante, I have to tell you…

729
01:13:27.666 --> 01:13:28.625
Hey, here they are.

730
01:13:29.625 --> 01:13:30.708
There they are!

731
01:13:35.125 --> 01:13:36.499
Our guests of honor.

732
01:13:36.500 --> 01:13:38.916
Come here, big guy. Great to see you.

733
01:13:42.833 --> 01:13:43.749
Yes.

734
01:13:43.750 --> 01:13:47.166
It doesn't hurt to ask, that's all I'm saying.

735
01:13:52.916 --> 01:13:54.833
But only after changing the tires.

736
01:13:56.916 --> 01:13:57.916
Okay.

737
01:13:58.916 --> 01:14:00.875
Oh, my God.

738
01:14:09.583 --> 01:14:11.083
I'm gonna use the restroom.

739
01:14:23.916 --> 01:14:25.208
What's up, spare?

740
01:14:25.791 --> 01:14:27.000
Hey, champ.

741
01:14:28.000 --> 01:14:30.875
It's probably no big deal, but…

742
01:14:32.000 --> 01:14:34.750
Was it you who drove the new best time on Eagle Track?

743
01:14:38.375 --> 01:14:39.208
During the day?

744
01:14:40.000 --> 01:14:41.958
Yeah, during the day.

745
01:14:44.916 --> 01:14:45.833
That's funny.

746
01:14:56.500 --> 01:15:00.957
Someone breaks your record in the dead of night, and no one says anything.

747
01:15:00.958 --> 01:15:04.165
Strange, isn't it? Not a word from the team.

748
01:15:04.166 --> 01:15:05.125
It wasn't me.

749
01:15:06.833 --> 01:15:07.833
Who was it?

750
01:15:12.208 --> 01:15:13.583
I like this wine.

751
01:15:14.875 --> 01:15:15.791
Hey, Jack!

752
01:15:17.791 --> 01:15:21.250
Ruben here thinks that someone broke my record in the night.

753
01:15:23.250 --> 01:15:24.291
Who was it?

754
01:15:31.583 --> 01:15:33.541
I'd like to know that, too.

755
01:15:41.583 --> 01:15:43.875
Okay, I…

756
01:15:44.958 --> 01:15:48.625
We didn't want to throw off your concentration, Dante, okay?

757
01:15:49.416 --> 01:15:52.875
This close to the season finale, you and your performance are the priority.

758
01:15:54.375 --> 01:15:56.708
That's why Sarah and I didn't tell you.

759
01:15:59.083 --> 01:16:00.291
Didn't tell me what?

760
01:16:03.000 --> 01:16:04.791
Sarah drove the new best time.

761
01:16:08.583 --> 01:16:12.957
She was incredibly fast. I've never seen anything like it in training.

762
01:16:12.958 --> 01:16:13.833
In training?

763
01:16:15.958 --> 01:16:17.333
Yeah.

764
01:16:19.250 --> 01:16:20.249
With you?

765
01:16:20.250 --> 01:16:25.000
Does that mean we're thinking that Sarah might become a driver?

766
01:16:27.250 --> 01:16:28.166
Dante…

767
01:16:30.333 --> 01:16:31.666
Dante, I…

768
01:16:35.458 --> 01:16:36.915
Dante, wait.

769
01:16:36.916 --> 01:16:38.208
Wait.

770
01:16:40.000 --> 01:16:41.791
- I wanted to tell you. - What?

771
01:16:43.291 --> 01:16:45.499
That Jack has been training you in secret?

772
01:16:45.500 --> 01:16:48.791
That they want to go behind my back and make you an Eagle driver?

773
01:16:50.000 --> 01:16:51.666
It's in case you leave.

774
01:16:54.416 --> 01:16:56.291
You've been playing me for a fool.

775
01:17:01.458 --> 01:17:02.291
Yes.

776
01:17:03.375 --> 01:17:05.333
Yes, I've been lying to you.

777
01:17:06.416 --> 01:17:10.750
But this is my big chance. Bronson's giving me an opportunity.

778
01:17:11.625 --> 01:17:13.708
- That means more to me than… - Than I do?

779
01:17:15.833 --> 01:17:17.582
Is that what you're trying to say?

780
01:17:17.583 --> 01:17:19.125
No, of course not, but…

781
01:17:22.875 --> 01:17:25.791
I couldn't have known that I'd fall in love with you.

782
01:17:27.833 --> 01:17:31.666
After this race, our business relationship is over.

783
01:17:33.458 --> 01:17:35.833
You get your money and I'll get some peace.

784
01:17:37.708 --> 01:17:38.708
Yes.

785
01:17:46.958 --> 01:17:48.041
Dante.

786
01:18:52.625 --> 01:18:55.540
What kind of spectacle are we in for today?

787
01:18:55.541 --> 01:19:01.374
80,000 tickets have been sold for the German Grand Prix, the Euro Masters,

788
01:19:01.375 --> 01:19:04.582
here in Donnersbach, on the traditional track.

789
01:19:04.583 --> 01:19:09.832
Yesterday, we saw the teams put together a very exciting qualifying session.

790
01:19:09.833 --> 01:19:15.416
Jakatomi, McKinnen and Annunziata all have a shot at the title.

791
01:19:16.208 --> 01:19:20.540
Annunziata is in pole position, leading the pack, and he has set the fastest time.

792
01:19:20.541 --> 01:19:24.540
He had a very strong qualifying session, and showed nerves of steel.

793
01:19:24.541 --> 01:19:27.415
But everything hinges on today.

794
01:19:27.416 --> 01:19:32.249
This story is being written live. Nothing is decided yet.

795
01:19:32.250 --> 01:19:36.082
And it's that uncertainty that makes this sport so attractive.

796
01:19:36.083 --> 01:19:40.958
Who can clinch the victory, here and now? Who is going to do it?

797
01:20:04.416 --> 01:20:07.000
We could always keep declining the interview.

798
01:20:07.666 --> 01:20:08.500
Why?

799
01:20:09.250 --> 01:20:10.708
It's part of the job.

800
01:20:17.958 --> 01:20:20.583
Okay, in that case we need to go.

801
01:20:21.125 --> 01:20:21.958
Right?

802
01:20:29.000 --> 01:20:30.707
Hello, Irene.

803
01:20:30.708 --> 01:20:32.082
Ruben?

804
01:20:32.083 --> 01:20:33.499
Long time.

805
01:20:33.500 --> 01:20:34.750
It's been forever.

806
01:20:36.250 --> 01:20:37.291
Is everything okay?

807
01:20:39.708 --> 01:20:41.499
Sarah's left already, right?

808
01:20:41.500 --> 01:20:42.666
Yes.

809
01:20:43.291 --> 01:20:44.791
Has something happened?

810
01:20:46.333 --> 01:20:47.750
Can I come in?

811
01:20:49.000 --> 01:20:51.832
Tell me, why can't Sarah know that you're here?

812
01:20:51.833 --> 01:20:55.125
Because she feels that she can handle things on her own.

813
01:20:57.375 --> 01:21:00.082
Lately, I haven't been able to get through to her at all.

814
01:21:00.083 --> 01:21:03.207
And that's exactly why we need to help her out of this.

815
01:21:03.208 --> 01:21:05.249
These people only think about themselves.

816
01:21:05.250 --> 01:21:08.166
They will drop her the moment she stops being useful to them.

817
01:21:08.875 --> 01:21:11.041
They did the same with me.

818
01:21:17.458 --> 01:21:20.666
I told her from the start that this deal wouldn't end well.

819
01:21:22.000 --> 01:21:23.708
What deal?

820
01:21:31.166 --> 01:21:32.625
Look.

821
01:21:35.333 --> 01:21:40.290
They're offering her 200,000 euros to pretend to be Dante's fiancée.

822
01:21:40.291 --> 01:21:42.583
- Weird, right? - For sure.

823
01:21:46.708 --> 01:21:47.541
See there.

824
01:21:52.541 --> 01:21:56.124
She forbade me from talking to anyone about it.

825
01:21:56.125 --> 01:21:57.916
Sure, this is explosive.

826
01:21:58.541 --> 01:22:00.250
Not a word to anybody.

827
01:22:01.041 --> 01:22:03.082
- Hello. Yes. - Great to see you.

828
01:22:03.083 --> 01:22:04.915
Nice to meet you, hello.

829
01:22:04.916 --> 01:22:06.250
Hello.

830
01:22:07.416 --> 01:22:10.540
- Please sit back there. - Thank you.

831
01:22:10.541 --> 01:22:12.500
I think that's a good spot.

832
01:22:14.500 --> 01:22:15.707
How lovely.

833
01:22:15.708 --> 01:22:17.875
I'm very excited to have you here.

834
01:22:19.500 --> 01:22:21.333
We're excited to be here.

835
01:22:22.291 --> 01:22:27.207
Dante, what is going through your head in the moments before this big finale?

836
01:22:27.208 --> 01:22:28.915
Not a lot.

837
01:22:28.916 --> 01:22:30.166
Oh, please.

838
01:22:31.708 --> 01:22:35.583
No, honestly. I'm totally focused on the race.

839
01:22:36.250 --> 01:22:38.666
Totally focused on the race.

840
01:22:40.208 --> 01:22:44.624
You two have turned into a regular power couple.

841
01:22:44.625 --> 01:22:48.500
How are you feeling about that, Sarah?

842
01:22:49.291 --> 01:22:51.624
All this attention all of a sudden.

843
01:22:51.625 --> 01:22:54.500
Your world is quite different from Dante's.

844
01:22:59.208 --> 01:23:00.541
I was…

845
01:23:02.500 --> 01:23:04.208
I am just…

846
01:23:07.166 --> 01:23:11.415
I am just very grateful for everything we have experienced together.

847
01:23:11.416 --> 01:23:13.333
What you have done with me.

848
01:23:17.500 --> 01:23:18.666
Sorry.

849
01:23:19.833 --> 01:23:22.749
Thanks to him, my world has changed a lot.

850
01:23:22.750 --> 01:23:28.082
The mechanic. The racing driver. Such great happiness.

851
01:23:28.083 --> 01:23:29.500
You could say that.

852
01:23:30.416 --> 01:23:32.541
It sounds like a modern-day fairy tale.

853
01:23:34.041 --> 01:23:39.416
And we all know what good fairy tales need.

854
01:23:40.333 --> 01:23:41.750
A good script.

855
01:23:45.125 --> 01:23:47.832
Or a water-tight contract.

856
01:23:47.833 --> 01:23:50.207
It's all written in here. Every word.

857
01:23:50.208 --> 01:23:53.999
Affection, kiss, discretion.

858
01:23:54.000 --> 01:23:57.082
- Stop. Excuse me. Could we… - And your name, right next to Sarah's.

859
01:23:57.083 --> 01:23:59.957
- Stop, can we cut? - Is this love?

860
01:23:59.958 --> 01:24:01.915
- Or just… - Can I see that?

861
01:24:01.916 --> 01:24:06.249
Okay, I know someone who knows about this kind of thing.

862
01:24:06.250 --> 01:24:08.540
I could take some photos and send them to him,

863
01:24:08.541 --> 01:24:10.457
just to be on the safe side, okay?

864
01:24:10.458 --> 01:24:11.375
Okay.

865
01:24:14.583 --> 01:24:18.833
Or is it all just a well-staged deal?

866
01:24:19.458 --> 01:24:22.083
Dear viewers, stay tuned.

867
01:24:23.916 --> 01:24:25.875
Fuck. What a pile of shit.

868
01:24:26.500 --> 01:24:28.874
- Where are you going? - To race.

869
01:24:28.875 --> 01:24:30.166
Shit.

870
01:24:31.000 --> 01:24:33.540
Shit, fucking shit.

871
01:24:33.541 --> 01:24:36.290
Interesting developments just minutes from the start.

872
01:24:36.291 --> 01:24:39.415
Dante Annunziata and Team Eagle have been accused

873
01:24:39.416 --> 01:24:41.624
of faking his relationship with Sarah Jenkins

874
01:24:41.625 --> 01:24:43.875
\to squash the scandal around the photo.

875
01:24:47.583 --> 01:24:48.874
One moment.

876
01:24:48.875 --> 01:24:50.708
You want to drive?

877
01:24:51.375 --> 01:24:52.416
I want to win.

878
01:24:53.291 --> 01:24:56.375
That's it. That's it. Exactly right. Go and win it.

879
01:24:57.791 --> 01:25:01.124
Yes, and will these accusations have an effect on Annunziata?

880
01:25:01.125 --> 01:25:04.083
His private life is a constant source of turmoil.

881
01:25:13.791 --> 01:25:18.165
Sweetie, I'm so sorry. Ruben was here. He said he wanted to help.

882
01:25:18.166 --> 01:25:21.124
He took pictures of the contract. He must be behind this.

883
01:25:21.125 --> 01:25:22.000
What?

884
01:25:26.500 --> 01:25:27.541
There you are.

885
01:25:30.541 --> 01:25:31.375
Why?

886
01:25:32.958 --> 01:25:34.583
Why did you do it?

887
01:25:36.500 --> 01:25:37.500
Why?

888
01:25:39.416 --> 01:25:44.208
Because I've been working my ass off for this team for four years!

889
01:25:46.083 --> 01:25:47.500
And what do I get?

890
01:25:49.666 --> 01:25:53.874
Bronson should have fired him for that photo of you two in the locker room.

891
01:25:53.875 --> 01:25:57.791
Instead, he can keep driving, and he gets…

892
01:26:01.708 --> 01:26:02.583
you?

893
01:26:06.833 --> 01:26:08.083
It was you.

894
01:26:16.500 --> 01:26:18.041
- Sarah, I… - No.

895
01:26:23.458 --> 01:26:24.500
Fuck you, Ruben.

896
01:26:26.833 --> 01:26:29.041
You just weren't fast enough.

897
01:26:44.875 --> 01:26:46.250
Hello. Thank you.

898
01:26:49.250 --> 01:26:51.540
- It surely can't get any worse today. - No.

899
01:26:51.541 --> 01:26:53.707
Great atmosphere here in Donnersbach.

900
01:26:53.708 --> 01:26:57.415
The fans here are almost as keyed-up as the drivers.

901
01:26:57.416 --> 01:27:00.625
Okay, and now go get the title. It belongs to you.

902
01:27:09.333 --> 01:27:13.666
It's nearly time now. The grand finale to a truly thrilling season.

903
01:27:24.958 --> 01:27:27.957
Doing well out of the straight, Annunziata takes the lead,

904
01:27:27.958 --> 01:27:30.125
aggressive driving from the get-go.

905
01:27:33.375 --> 01:27:34.541
Yeah!

906
01:27:46.125 --> 01:27:49.915
Lap 15. Annunziata is confidently building up his lead.

907
01:27:49.916 --> 01:27:53.541
He's now got a 12-second lead over Paulsen in second place.

908
01:28:01.041 --> 01:28:03.374
Okay, pit lane, Dante! Your tires are worn.

909
01:28:03.375 --> 01:28:04.957
No, not yet!

910
01:28:04.958 --> 01:28:06.957
Dante, the tires are about to blow.

911
01:28:06.958 --> 01:28:08.291
Your race, your call.

912
01:28:16.958 --> 01:28:17.916
No.

913
01:28:22.291 --> 01:28:25.624
21st lap. Suddenly Annunziata's car skids.

914
01:28:25.625 --> 01:28:28.707
What's this? Contact with the barriers. Totally unnecessary.

915
01:28:28.708 --> 01:28:31.790
What's up with Annunziata? Is it his nerves or is it the tires?

916
01:28:31.791 --> 01:28:34.290
He's the only driver not to have changed tires yet.

917
01:28:34.291 --> 01:28:37.332
Yes, a very questionable strategy decision for Eagle Racing.

918
01:28:37.333 --> 01:28:38.625
I'm coming in.

919
01:28:56.000 --> 01:28:57.000
Dante, what's up?

920
01:28:58.375 --> 01:28:59.540
Dante?

921
01:28:59.541 --> 01:29:01.625
I… I can't do it.

922
01:29:02.166 --> 01:29:04.207
What can't you do? What's wrong?

923
01:29:04.208 --> 01:29:07.624
What do you mean, you can't? You're in the lead!

924
01:29:07.625 --> 01:29:10.040
Is this the turning point for Eagle Racing?

925
01:29:10.041 --> 01:29:13.041
His lead is evaporating! Annunziata isn't leaving the pit.

926
01:29:16.291 --> 01:29:17.250
Hey!

927
01:29:19.000 --> 01:29:19.833
Dante.

928
01:29:25.375 --> 01:29:26.333
Do it for her.

929
01:29:27.458 --> 01:29:29.958
Do it for the angel with the bloody knees.

930
01:29:34.250 --> 01:29:35.833
Dante, what's going on? Drive!

931
01:29:40.375 --> 01:29:44.332
Annunziata is back in the race! Paulsen's in first, Jakatomi in second.

932
01:29:44.333 --> 01:29:47.291
What a thriller. This finale is always tense.

933
01:29:54.041 --> 01:29:58.083
Annunziata working bravely on the outside. A world-class overtaking maneu…

934
01:30:16.083 --> 01:30:17.666
Four seconds to Paulsen.

935
01:30:24.541 --> 01:30:26.291
Two seconds to Paulsen.

936
01:30:38.666 --> 01:30:39.708
Do it!

937
01:31:45.833 --> 01:31:48.540
He's done it! It's crazy!

938
01:31:48.541 --> 01:31:49.540
Yes! Yes!

939
01:31:49.541 --> 01:31:53.332
Annunziata wins the German Grand Prix in Donnersbach.

940
01:31:53.333 --> 01:31:55.583
Against all odds! Incredible!

941
01:32:12.250 --> 01:32:15.208
You did it, son! You did it!

942
01:32:18.208 --> 01:32:19.666
You did it!

943
01:32:20.458 --> 01:32:22.125
You did it, Dante.

944
01:32:22.875 --> 01:32:24.791
- Dante. - We did it.

945
01:32:26.375 --> 01:32:28.416
We did it. We did it.

946
01:33:08.375 --> 01:33:12.583
Dante Annunziata!

947
01:33:24.500 --> 01:33:25.416
Sarah!

948
01:33:28.041 --> 01:33:29.083
Sarah!

949
01:33:30.291 --> 01:33:32.665
I was just up on the podium,

950
01:33:32.666 --> 01:33:35.166
but for the first time ever, I didn't care.

951
01:33:36.500 --> 01:33:38.624
I just wanted to be here.

952
01:33:38.625 --> 01:33:39.625
With you.

953
01:34:06.083 --> 01:34:06.916
Now what?

954
01:34:07.875 --> 01:34:09.125
Do we drive off?

955
01:34:10.416 --> 01:34:11.250
Why not?

956
01:34:14.583 --> 01:34:15.541
You drive.

957
01:34:23.791 --> 01:34:24.916
Okay, hop in!

958
01:34:28.291 --> 01:34:30.832
So, people, at first, it was a fake love story

959
01:34:30.833 --> 01:34:32.665
and then it turned into real love.

960
01:34:32.666 --> 01:34:35.707
I knew all along that it was for real.

961
01:34:35.708 --> 01:34:37.624
Their love never seemed fake to me.

962
01:34:37.625 --> 01:34:39.540
It was real the whole time.

963
01:34:39.541 --> 01:34:42.790
Is this true love, or just a contractual requirement?

964
01:34:42.791 --> 01:34:45.750
People, where are Sarah and Dante?

965
01:34:56.083 --> 01:34:56.958
Sarah, hi!

966
01:34:57.375 --> 01:34:59.999
I've been trying to reach you for days. Where are you?

967
01:35:00.000 --> 01:35:04.749
If, by chance, you're still alive and interested in your career, listen to me.

968
01:35:04.750 --> 01:35:08.374
We want you, not as a marketing gimmick, but as a driver.

969
01:35:08.375 --> 01:35:09.957
Eagle's new number one.

970
01:35:09.958 --> 01:35:12.082
I haven't heard from Dante. Just rumors.

971
01:35:12.083 --> 01:35:14.874
An offer from Formula 1 maybe. Whatever. Don't care.

972
01:35:14.875 --> 01:35:17.665
It's about you now. This is your big chance.

973
01:35:17.666 --> 01:35:19.375
Call me back. We need to talk.

974
01:35:29.916 --> 01:35:30.750
Hey.

975
01:35:32.916 --> 01:35:35.041
I think you should accept.

976
01:35:40.791 --> 01:35:41.875
What about you?

977
01:35:43.333 --> 01:35:45.540
Maybe I don't want to do Formula 1 anymore

978
01:35:45.541 --> 01:35:47.416
after you've signed.

979
01:35:48.833 --> 01:35:51.332
- And instead? - I stay and look forward

980
01:35:51.333 --> 01:35:52.791
to seeing your pretty smile…

981
01:35:53.416 --> 01:35:54.708
in the rearview mirror.

982
01:35:57.416 --> 01:35:58.458
You wish.
